{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 39, :comments ["<b>However, on the fifteenth day.</b> After mentioning the general matters common to all the festivals — namely that they are all מִקְרָאֵי קֹדֶשׁ and require an additional offering, as it says: אֵלֶּה מוֹעֲדֵי ה׳ אֲשֶׁר תִּקְרְאוּ אֹתָם מִקְרָאֵי קֹדֶשׁ לְהַקְרִיב אִשֶּׁה (Leviticus 23:37) — He said, אַךְ בַּחֲמִשָּׁה עָשָׂר יוֹם, and informed us that the festival of Sukkot is distinguished from the other festivals: first, in that its eighth day is מִקְרָא קֹדֶשׁ, as it says <b>and on the eighth day a solemn rest</b> — not so for the days of the week and the days of the festival of Matzot, and likewise for the months and the years in which the seventh is holy, not the eighth. Second, in that this festival requires a change of dwelling, as it says: בַּסֻּכֹּת תֵּשְׁבוּ (Leviticus 23:42). Third, in that it requires the waving of the four species, as it says: וּלְקַחְתֶּם לָכֶם בַּיּוֹם הָרִאשׁוֹן פְּרִי עֵץ הָדָר (Leviticus 23:40)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:37:37.672694464Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}